From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:30:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: exynos: Let an SoC act just before the post link
 calibration

The PHY is calibrated once the link is up, and that call is made by the
shared code before the SoC gets its turn.  An SoC whose calibration has
to be bracketed by writes that go over the link itself cannot do it from
either hook it has: the one before the link is too early, the one after
runs when the calibration is already done.

Add a hook that runs immediately before it.  Nothing sets it yet, so no
SoC changes behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c | 3 +++
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.h | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
index e9bd59648a9..12fd8bbb230 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
@@ -1247,6 +1247,9 @@ static int exynos_ufs_post_link(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 		}
 	}
 
+	if (ufs->drv_data->pre_phy_cal)
+		ufs->drv_data->pre_phy_cal(ufs);
+
 	phy_calibrate(generic_phy);
 
 	if (ufs->drv_data->post_link)
diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.h b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.h
index abe7e472759..30d7882e85e 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.h
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.h
@@ -185,6 +185,12 @@ struct exynos_ufs_drv_data {
 	/* SoC's specific operations */
 	int (*drv_init)(struct exynos_ufs *ufs);
 	int (*pre_link)(struct exynos_ufs *ufs);
+	/*
+	 * Runs once the link is up and just before the PHY is calibrated for
+	 * it, which is the only place from which that calibration can be
+	 * bracketed by writes that go over the link itself.
+	 */
+	int (*pre_phy_cal)(struct exynos_ufs *ufs);
 	int (*post_link)(struct exynos_ufs *ufs);
 	int (*pre_pwr_change)(struct exynos_ufs *ufs,
 				struct ufs_pa_layer_attr *pwr);
